# the keys transposed: F minor puts F on the C key; the step editor (SEQ's third row on the piano): K1 walks, K2 a note
# in / a third on it / out, K3 a tie up to the cursor and a cut, K4 the pitch, a key at the cursor, the undo
wait 300
expect keyw4 60
tap EDIT
wait 50
turn K1 5
turn K2 1
wait 50
expect root 5
expect keyw4 65
expect keyw5 67
expect keyw6 68
turn K2 -1
turn K1 -5
wait 50
expect keyw4 60
# the piano's clip emptied, the step editor
press HOME
tapkey b0
release HOME
tap SEQ
wait 50
# the EDIT list: ERASE NOTES (white 12) twice, then back to SEQ
page 11
tap EDIT
tapkey w11
tapkey w11
page 1
wait 50
expect events 0
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
wait 50
expect cursor 0
turn K2 1
wait 50
expect events 1
expect senotes 1
expect selen 1
turn K2 1
wait 50
expect senotes 2
turn K2 -1
wait 50
expect senotes 1
expect events 1
turn K1 3
wait 50
expect cursor 3
expect senotes 0
turn K3 1
wait 50
turn K1 -3
wait 50
expect selen 4
turn K1 5
turn K3 1
wait 50
